return [
    [
        'type' => 'post',
        'key' => 'indian-importers-guide-to-importing-from-china-compliance-certifications-practical-alternatives-2026',
        'title' => 'Import from China to India: Documents, Licences & Steps',
        'description' => 'How to import from China to India in 2026: step-by-step process, documents checklist, BIS/WPC/LMPC/EPR rules by product, duties and what gets shipments stuck.',
        'answer' => '<p><strong>To import from China to India you need an Importer Exporter Code (IEC), the product approvals that apply to your goods (BIS, WPC, LMPC, EPR and others), and a complete set of shipping documents: commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading or airway bill, and a bill of entry filed with Indian Customs.</strong> The seven steps, the documents checklist and the approvals by product category are below.</p>',
        'top' => [
            ['How to import from China to India in 7 steps', '<ol>
<li><strong>Get your IEC.</strong> Apply on the DGFT portal with the PAN of your business. It is issued online, and you cannot import commercially without it. See <a href="/services/indian-registration-compliances/import-export/import-export-code-iec">IEC registration</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Check the product’s approvals before you pay the supplier.</strong> Find the HS code, then check whether it needs <a href="/certification/india/bis-crs-mark-certification">BIS CRS registration</a> or an ISI licence, <a href="/certification/india/wpc-eta-approval">WPC ETA approval</a>, <a href="/certification/india/tec-approval">TEC</a>, <a href="/services/indian-registration-compliances/business-licenses/lmpc-for-packaging">LMPC registration</a>, EPR, FSSAI or CDSCO. Most stuck shipments start here.</li>
<li><strong>Register on ICEGATE if you will file yourself.</strong> <a href="/services/indian-registration-compliances/import-export/icegate-registration">ICEGATE registration</a> lets you file and track customs documents online. Many importers let a licensed customs broker file for them instead.</li>
<li><strong>Agree terms with the supplier.</strong> Fix the Incoterm (FOB, CIF or EXW), the payment method, and the labelling your goods need for India: importer name and address, MRP and the other Legal Metrology declarations.</li>
<li><strong>Book freight and insurance.</strong> A freight forwarder arranges sea (FCL or LCL) or air shipment and issues or collects the bill of lading or airway bill.</li>
<li><strong>File the bill of entry and pay duty.</strong> The bill of entry is filed on ICEGATE, customs assesses duty on the assessable value, and duty is paid online.</li>
<li><strong>Clear and take delivery.</strong> If the shipment is selected for examination, customs checks the goods against your documents. After the out-of-charge order, the goods leave the port or container freight station.</li>
</ol>'],
            ['Documents required to import from China', '<table><thead><tr><th>Document</th><th>Who provides it</th><th>Why customs needs it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Commercial invoice</td><td>Chinese supplier</td><td>Shows the value, currency and terms on which duty is assessed</td></tr>
<tr><td>Packing list</td><td>Chinese supplier</td><td>Quantities, weights and package marks, used during examination</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bill of lading or airway bill</td><td>Shipping line, airline or forwarder</td><td>Proof of shipment and title to the goods</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bill of entry</td><td>Importer or customs broker, on ICEGATE</td><td>The customs declaration for the import</td></tr>
<tr><td>IEC</td><td>Importer, from DGFT</td><td>Required for every commercial import</td></tr>
<tr><td>Product approvals</td><td>Manufacturer or importer</td><td>BIS registration or licence, WPC ETA, LMPC, EPR, FSSAI or CDSCO, where the product needs them</td></tr>
<tr><td>Certificate of origin</td><td>Supplier or a Chinese issuing body</td><td>Needed to claim a preferential duty rate, for example under the Asia-Pacific Trade Agreement, or when customs asks</td></tr>
<tr><td>Insurance certificate and payment proof</td><td>Insurer and bank</td><td>Supports the declared value</td></tr>
</tbody></table>'],
            ['Certifications by product category', '<table><thead><tr><th>Product category</th><th>What usually applies in India</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Electronics and IT (chargers, adapters, laptops, LED lights, power banks)</td><td>BIS CRS registration with an R-number for listed products; WPC ETA for Wi-Fi or Bluetooth; TEC (MTCTE) for telecom equipment; e-waste EPR; LMPC for retail packs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Toys</td><td>BIS ISI licence under IS 9873 and IS 15644, held by the manufacturing factory</td></tr>
<tr><td>Steel products</td><td>BIS ISI licence for grades covered by the steel Quality Control Orders, held by the mill</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chemicals and polymers</td><td>BIS ISI where a Quality Control Order covers the chemical (the list changes often, so check it for your HS code), MSDS, and plastic EPR for packaging</td></tr>
<tr><td>Food and food ingredients</td><td>FSSAI Central licence for importers and FSSAI import clearance for each consignment</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cosmetics and medical devices</td><td>CDSCO import registration or licence</td></tr>
<tr><td>Batteries</td><td>BIS CRS registration for listed cells and batteries, and battery EPR</td></tr>
<tr><td>Packaged consumer goods</td><td>LMPC importer registration and correct label declarations</td></tr>
</tbody></table>'],
            ['Can you import any product from China?', '<p>No. Most goods are <strong>free</strong> to import under India’s ITC (HS) import policy, but some are <strong>restricted</strong> and need a DGFT import authorisation, some are <strong>prohibited</strong>, and a few can only be imported through state trading enterprises. Check the policy condition for your HS code before you order.</p><p>A product that is free to import can still need a product approval (BIS, WPC, FSSAI and so on) and can attract anti-dumping duty, which India applies to many Chinese goods. Second-hand goods, such as used electronics and machinery, have their own conditions.</p>'],
            ['Common reasons shipments get stuck at customs', '<ul>
<li>The model, brand or factory is not covered by the BIS registration or licence, or the BIS mark and R-number are missing from the product.</li>
<li>A radio product has no WPC ETA, or a telecom product has no TEC certificate.</li>
<li>Retail packs lack Legal Metrology declarations such as the importer’s name and address, MRP or net quantity.</li>
<li>The declared value is lower than customs expects, or the HS code is wrong.</li>
<li>Anti-dumping duty applies and was not provided for.</li>
<li>The importer has no EPR registration for plastic packaging, e-waste or batteries.</li>
<li>Food samples fail, or labels do not meet FSSAI rules.</li>
<li>The invoice, packing list and bill of lading do not match each other.</li>
</ul>'],
        ],
        'faqs' => [
            ['Can I import from China to India as an individual?', 'Yes. Goods for personal use can be imported without an IEC, subject to customs duty and the baggage or courier rules. To import for sale you need an IEC, which an individual can get as a sole proprietor using their own PAN.'],
            ['Is BIS needed for all Chinese products?', 'No. BIS registration or a BIS licence is needed only for products covered by the Compulsory Registration Scheme or by a Quality Control Order. Check your product’s HS code and description against the current lists before you place the order.'],
            ['How much duty is charged on imports from China?', 'It depends on the HS code. The usual components are basic customs duty, a social welfare surcharge on that duty, and IGST on the value plus duties, with anti-dumping duty added where it has been notified for the product. The current rates are in the customs tariff on the CBIC and ICEGATE websites.'],
            ['How long does customs clearance take?', 'When documents are complete and the shipment is not selected for examination, clearance usually takes a few working days after the goods arrive. It takes longer when goods are examined, when samples are drawn for testing, or when customs raises a query on value or classification.'],
        ],
