            ['How long does an FSSAI licence take?', '<p>Basic registration is usually granted within 7 to 30 days, depending on whether the officer inspects the premises. State and Central licences are decided within 60 days of a complete application, and later if an inspection or a query is raised. Read <a href="/resources/blogs/how-much-time-it-takes-to-get-fssai-license">how much time it takes to get an FSSAI licence</a> for the stage-by-stage timeline.</p>'],
        ],
        'faqs' => [
            ['What is the meaning of FSSAI?', 'FSSAI means the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, the national food regulator. On a food pack, the FSSAI logo with a 14-digit number means the business that made or sold the food is registered or licensed with FSSAI.'],
            ['What is the long form of FSSAI in Hindi?', 'In Hindi, FSSAI is भारतीय खाद्य सुरक्षा और मानक प्राधिकरण (Bharatiya Khadya Suraksha aur Manak Pradhikaran). The English long form is Food Safety and Standards Authority of India.'],
            ['Is FSSAI mandatory for a home food business?', 'Yes. Every food business, including home kitchens, home bakers and tiffin services, needs at least FSSAI Basic registration. If turnover goes above ₹12 lakh a year, a State licence is needed.'],
            ['Who heads FSSAI?', 'FSSAI is headed by a Chairperson, with a Chief Executive Officer who runs it day to day. Both are appointed by the Central Government; the current office-holders are listed on fssai.gov.in.'],
