        'faqs' => [
            ['What is the full form of BOCW?', 'BOCW stands for Building and Other Construction Workers. It refers to the construction workers’ laws of 1996, whose provisions moved into the OSH Code and the Code on Social Security from 21 November 2025.'],
            ['What is a BOCW certificate?', 'It is usually the registration certificate the state labour department issues to an employer for a construction establishment. Construction workers also get a registration card from the state welfare board, which is sometimes called a BOCW certificate.'],
            ['What are the BOCW registration fees?', 'Each state sets the fee in its rules, based on the number of workers employed, and it is paid online with the application. It is separate from the 1% cess on the cost of construction.'],
            ['Who pays the BOCW cess?', 'The employer carrying out the construction work pays the cess, at 1% of the cost of construction. On government projects it is usually deducted from the contractor’s bills and paid to the state welfare board.'],
